# Campus Connect frontend

Read `frontend/FRONTEND_SPEC.md` before making visual changes — it records the measured
dimensions, colour tokens and typography scale this UI is built from.

## The reference design is authoritative

The UI reproduces a reference design screenshot. For anything visual, match the
reference rather than personal taste, and measure instead of guessing. Do not redesign,
simplify, or introduce a competing visual system.

## Stack

Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + `lucide-react` + `framer-motion`.

- Prefer custom Tailwind components. Do not add a component library, state manager,
  data layer, or second icon set.
- Avoid new dependencies generally — a small local SVG beats a package.
- Use the `@theme` tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. Add a token rather than hard-coding
  the same new colour twice.
- `globals.css` is for body defaults, font smoothing, the global background, box-sizing
  and shared tokens only. Component styling belongs in Tailwind utilities.

## Structure

- `app/page.tsx` composes the shell and holds only panel-visibility state. Keep event
  data, map markup and component-specific styling out of it.
- Keep components small and focused. No giant files, no duplicate components, no
  speculative abstraction.
- Strict TypeScript; avoid `any`.

## No backend code in visual components

Visual components take plain props. Keep data fetching, side effects and persistence out
of them — in server components or dedicated hooks when they arrive.

The current phase is presentation-only: no API calls, database access, auth,
geolocation, notifications, persistence, real search or real filtering. Buttons may have
hover and press states without production behaviour. Do not implement these early.

## The map will be replaced by Mapbox

`components/map/CampusMapPlaceholder.tsx` is the seam. It accepts
`{ events, selectedEventId, onSelectEvent }` — the props a real map needs — so Mapbox can
drop in behind the same interface.

`CampusMapArt.tsx` is the throwaway static illustration. It must be imported only by the
placeholder and must never leak into unrelated components.

Keep the map desaturated so event markers stay the most saturated thing on screen.

## Assets are local only

No remote images: no Unsplash, Pexels, randomuser.me, or CDN avatars. Use local SVG, CSS
compositions, or files under `public/assets/`. The app must render with zero network
image requests.

## Motion

Subtle and premium: short hover transitions, a 1px lift on pills, a small scale-down on
press, a marker hover scale around 1.08, and the drawer slide. No constant bouncing or
pulsing, no large scaling, rotations, or dramatic transitions.

## Definition of done

`npm run build` passes from `frontend/`, with no TypeScript errors, no lint-related build
blockers, and no browser console errors.
